  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Question": "What is the range of the eccentricity of an ellipse?",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "Greater than \\(1\\)",
    "B": "Greater than \\(0\\) and less than \\(1\\)",
    "C": "Equal to \\(1\\)",
    "D": "Less than \\(0\\)"
  },
  "Correct Answer": "B",
  "Accepted Answers": [],
  "Unordered Answers": false,
  "Solution": "Under the noncircular ellipse convention, let \\(a>b>0\\) be the semiaxis lengths and let \\(c\\) be the distance from the center to a focus. The relation \\(c^2=a^2-b^2\\) gives \\(0<c<a\\), so \\(0<e=c/a<1\\). Under this convention the answer is B. The closer \\(e\\) is to \\(1\\), the flatter the ellipse is.\n\nIf circles are included as ellipses, \\(a=b>0\\) gives \\(c=0\\) and \\(e=0\\), as for \\(x^2+y^2=1\\). The range is then \\(0\\le e<1\\), and none of the choices gives that range.",
